==Enemy==
This enemy, while not too durable, has extremely powerful Long Distance Area Attacks, strong enough to destroy most units in one hit. Fortunately, Hackey has an extremely large blind spot of 1200, with his standing range being well within it, meaning most units can sneak inside due to his long attack delay.

==Strategy==
Hackey acts like a unit speed-check, instantly destroying any units that are too slow to enter his large blind spot. Make sure to time your attackers perfectly to minimize Hackey's destruction. Much of the same strategies that work against the original Tackey should also work against this enemy, but you '''do not''' want him getting a hit off on any of your important units. Luring can work, but be careful not to let him get too close to the [[Cat Base]], because even a maxed base can only withstand four fastballs from this fiery pitcher at 100% magnification.

He usually has multiple melee units to push cats out of his blind spot. If you have any long distance units, such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife]] or [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], that sit inside Hackey's range, they could destroy Hackey to let units that sit outside his blind spot or are too slow to enter could get in and help the other attackers.

