==Trivia==
*Hackey's name may be a combination of ''hacha'' (a Spanish word that primarily means axe, but could also refer to a kind of torch or large candle, a kind of wind-resistant wick or fuse made of esparto and tar, or someone who is especially skilled in a particular field), ''hack up'' (to expel something by coughing, referencing how Hackey's projectiles come from his mouth) and ''[[Tackey]]''.
*Hackey's Japanese name, Hiuma, is derived from 火 ''hi'', meaning "fire", and ''[[wikia:kyojin-no-hoshi:Hyūma Hoshi|Hyūma Hoshi]]'', a hotblooded aspiring pitcher and protagonist of the classic baseball manga [[wikipedia:Star of the Giants|''Star of the Giants'']].  His flaming eyes are a reference to how [[wikia:kyojin-no-hoshi:Iconic Kyojin no Hoshi scenes that are mostly parodied#Hyūma Hoshi's Burning Eyes|Hyūma's eyes]] tend to burn with flames of passion when he gets heated up.
**Hiuma could also be a pun on 海馬 ''umiuma'', one of the Japanese words for seahorse.
*As a seahorse with an affinity for fire, Hackey may have been inspired by the myth that seahorses are born from dragons or become dragons after a long time. In fact, one of the Japanese words for seahorse, 竜の落とし子 ''tatsu no otoshigo'', literally translates to "dragon's illegitimate child".
*The word 魔球 ''makyū'' in his Japanese description refers to an unhittable [[wikipedia:breaking ball|breaking ball]], but can literally be taken as "demon ball" or "magic ball".
*Both Hackey's English and Japanese descriptions play off of the term "benchwarmer", which refers to a sports player that is almost never selected to play during games, thus spending most of their time sitting on the team's bench, keeping it warm.

